I have spent 7 years at various roles in NVIDIA. 

Currently I work in the Denver ARM CPU JIT/Runtime team and in addition am also responsible for performance tweaking all layers of the Android stack, from the kernel to V8/Mozilla JITs in order to get the best out of Denver.

Prior to this, I was the Architect of Project Orion, which focussed on providing Unified Virtual Memory between cache coherent ARM CPU and Kepler GPU for CUDA programs. Before that I spent 5 years in the GPU kernel team, specializing in Memory Management, Thread Scheduling, Latency control, Interrupt and was the Kernel Dev Lead for Fermi Architecture.

Outside work, my passion is in Locks, MultiThreading, Parallel Computing and very recently, completed development on Query Processor (Khronos) that takes in Serial C-like code and Auto-Parallelizes it for MultiCore Execution. Details and other projects along with source at www.pseudoparallel.com


